{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Living at Ease: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja10'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 10 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Apaṇṇakavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sure Bet </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>10. Sukhavihārijātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Living at Ease: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yañca aññe na rakkhanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>He who is not guarded by others, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yo ca aññe na rakkhati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and who does not guard others, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sa ve rāja sukhaṁ seti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>truly sleeps at ease, O King, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kāmesu anapekkhavā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>unconcerned for sensual pleasures. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Sukhavihārijātakaṁ dasamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Apaṇṇakavaggo paṭhamo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Varāpaṇṇaka vaṇṇupatha serivaro, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Suvicakkhaṇa taṇḍulanāḷikassā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Hiri puttavaruttagāmaṇinā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo ca na rakkhati tena dasāti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
